{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "6c1b8a51-9f0e-4c39-9a4e-1d0e7a5c2f10",
    "name": "Lowtides: AI spend governor",
    "description": "One budget and a STOP button between AI agents and money.\n\nRun folders 1-4 in order with the Collection Runner against the public demo (https://lowtides.ai, PayPal sandbox, simulated models, no password) or your own copy. Each run makes its own agent.\n\n1. Setup: create an agent, add a merchant, write the rules in plain English.\n2. Agent: the agent checks its budget, makes a model call, and asks before buying. Tests assert each decision.\n3. Dashboard: a person approves, denies and KILLs.\n4. Webhooks: send events to a Zapier Catch Hook.\n5. STOP ALL (optional; stops every agent).\n\nOpenAPI: {{baseUrl}}/openapi.json. Docs: https://github.com/seniorhelper/lowtides",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Setup (dashboard)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create a test agent",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Admin-Token",
                "value": "{{adminToken}}",
                "description": "Dashboard password. Leave empty for the public demo."
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/agents",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "agents"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Makes a fresh agent for this run and saves its key (agentKey) and id (agentId).",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Postman agent {{$timestamp}}\",\n  \"daily_budget\": 5\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"HTTP 200\", () => { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"agent created with a Lowtides key\", () => { pm.expect(j.agent.key).to.match(/^lt-/); pm.expect(j.agent.status).to.eql(\"on\"); });",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"agentKey\", j.agent.key);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"agentId\", j.agent.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Add a known merchant (PayPal payee)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Admin-Token",
                "value": "{{adminToken}}",
                "description": "Dashboard password. Leave empty for the public demo."
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/merchants",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "merchants"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Purchases from known merchants can be auto-approved. New payees always wait for a person.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Acme Data\",\n  \"paypal_email\": \"merchant-demo@example.com\",\n  \"category\": \"data\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"HTTP 200\", () => { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"merchant saved\", () => { pm.expect(j.merchant.name).to.eql(\"Acme Data\"); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Rules in plain English",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Admin-Token",
                "value": "{{adminToken}}",
                "description": "Dashboard password. Leave empty for the public demo."
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/rules/compile",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "rules",
                "compile"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Does not save. A person reviews the rules first; the AI never decides a payment.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"text\": \"Max $100 a day. No more than $60 per purchase. Ask me over $25. Never buy gift cards or crypto.\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"HTTP 200\", () => { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"Claude (or the offline parser) turned it into strict rules\", () => { pm.expect(j.rules.max_per_purchase).to.eql(60); pm.expect(j.rules.approval_over).to.eql(25); pm.expect(j.rules.daily_purchase_limit).to.eql(100); pm.expect(j.rules.blocked_categories).to.include(\"gift cards\"); });",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"compiledRules\", JSON.stringify(j.rules));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Save the rules",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Admin-Token",
                "value": "{{adminToken}}",
                "description": "Dashboard password. Leave empty for the public demo."
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/agents/{{agentId}}/rules",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "agents",
                "{{agentId}}",
                "rules"
              ]
            },
            "description": "",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\"rules\": {{compiledRules}}}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"HTTP 200\", () => { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"rules saved\", () => { pm.expect(j.rules.approval_over).to.eql(25); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
